Apologies in advance for posting direct to the list:

I had the same problem with this patch, but in this instance the patch =
kitting is actually correct.

The problem is with the HP 'patch alert' email bulletin that was sent =
out, which for the third time this year has the PK3 and PK4 URL's for a =
patch transposed with their respective descriptions.

You'll see in the HP email URL from the original posting that the base =
level is BB26 - which indicates the patch is written for OS PK5 AKA =
Tru64 5.1b-3, not 5.1b-4 per the description in the HP email.

The correct BB27 patch for OS PK6 AKA Tru64 5.1b-4 is available at the =
following URL:
http://www.itrc.hp.com/service/patch/patchDetail.do?patchid=3DT64KIT10012=
05-V51BB27-ES-20070427


