I have an OpenVMS 8.2 server running an unsupported version of Sybase client connecting into a Tru64 sybase server.  Everything works fine connecting into a Tru64 51.b machine.  We are now trying to replace the Tru64 machine with an hp-ux machine and we are having Sybase connection issues.  The errors seem to be related to sockets.  I found another site that said to look at the following output from hp-ux:
 
 sysdef | egrep "NAME|ninode|nfile|maxfiles_lim"
NAME                      VALUE       BOOT        MIN-MAX        UNITS
FLAGS
maxfiles_lim               4096          -         30-2048
-
nfile                     65536          -         14-
-
ninode                     4880          -         14-
 
Does anyone know what the command would be to run something like this on the Tru64 machine?  Has anyone seen something like this before?  
 
I would like to compare the values between the two machines.  
 
Thanks,
 
Howard


